Tolerate client disconnect in RPC reply path

Three RPC handlers (`monitor`, `list_tests`, `run_test`) finish by
sending the response to the client and calling `.unwrap()` on the
result. When the client's WebSocket has already closed (Ctrl-C,
`cargo run` exiting after flash, network blip), the reply returns
`Err(ConnectionClosed)`, the unwrap panics, and the tokio worker
dies without releasing the held probe `Session`. systemd does not
restart the service because the panic is contained inside one
worker, so the probe is left in a stale "in use" state that
manifests on the next client as a silent exit-0 with no flash.

Discard the result instead of unwrapping; a closed client is the
expected case at the end of every RPC and is not actionable here.

Local fix only; no upstream issue or PR exists yet.

--- a/probe-rs-tools/src/bin/probe-rs/rpc/functions/monitor.rs
+++ b/probe-rs-tools/src/bin/probe-rs/rpc/functions/monitor.rs
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@
     sender
         .reply::<MonitorEndpoint>(header.seq_no, &resp)
         .await
-        .unwrap();
+        .ok();
 }

